# 🛍 E-Commerce Price Scraper - Mini Project

This project is a B.Tech mini project that allows users to scrape product prices (e.g., iPhone 16 128GB) from major Indian e-commerce websites including:

- Amazon.in
- Flipkart.com
- Croma.com
- RelianceDigital.in

Built with **Python**, **Selenium**, **BeautifulSoup**, and **FastAPI**, it provides a unified way to get real-time product pricing across platforms.

---

## 📁 Project Structure

web_scrapping/ │ ├── amazon_scraper.py # Scrapes product data from Amazon ├── flipkart_scraper.py # Scrapes product data from Flipkart ├── croma_scraper.py # Scrapes product data from Croma ├── reliance_scraper.py # Scrapes product data from Reliance Digital │ ├── main.py # FastAPI server with combined route ├── utils.py # Shared utility functions ├── requirements.txt # Required Python packages └── README.md # You're reading it!

yaml
Copy
Edit

---

## 🚀 Features

✅ Scrape live prices, titles, and links for a search term
✅ Combines results from all four platforms
✅ Headless and visual scraping support
✅ Built-in popup handling (e.g., Reliance Digital)
✅ FastAPI endpoint to trigger scraping via browser or API

---

## 🧰 Installation

Install dependencies:
pip install -r requirements.txt

Run the FastAPI server:
uvicorn main:app --reload
Access the API Docs:

Visit http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

📝 Usage Example
Call the endpoint /scrape?query=iphone+16+128gb to get a list of matching products:
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/scrape?query=iphone+16+128gb

📌 Notes
Amazon and Flipkart layouts may change frequently, keep your XPaths updated.
Reliance Digital may show popups — the scraper handles common ones.
This project is for educational purposes only.